{"type":"say","text":"Good question, Omar. Let's keep automatic-merge-after-CI as a shared provision for both categories for now — the current draft already requires approval(s) before merge, and auto-merge just means the merge happens automatically once CI passes after those approvals are in place. For regulated repos, the 2-approval requirement still has to be satisfied before auto-merge triggers, so the additional control is already baked in. If your compliance review finds that CI-gated auto-merge needs further restrictions for regulated repos, we can revisit before Monday, but I don't want to block the split on that question today.

Tess, that's helpful — naming the fallback group 'eng-oncall' and requiring an alert on unresolved ownership gives us a concrete operational spec we can write into the policy. Please file the cleanup ticket for those six repos today so we have a tracked remediation path.

Before I make a final decision, I still need to hear from the remaining functional owners on the checklist. Are there any other blockers or concerns from security, legal, or other areas we haven't heard from yet?"}

